---
/* generate_report: digest for the last N days — traffic, 5xx rate, top
   countries/paths/networks, firewall activity, alerts, changes made — with
   printable HTML and CSV per table (app/api/reports/zone/route.ts). */
---
<section class="report-sec" id="report">
  <div class="wrap report-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="sc">Report</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:12px">The Friday report, in one sentence.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:18px;font-size:15.5px">
        <em>"Send me a seven-day digest for client.com."</em> Back comes the
        window in prose — traffic, error rate, where it came from, what the
        firewall did, which alerts fired, and every change anyone made — with a
        printable page for the client and a CSV for every table. Incidents get
        the same treatment: each one a page of its own, with what fired, what
        was found, and what was done.
      </p>
      <ul class="fit" style="margin-top:22px">
        <li>Highlights written for a client, not an engineer</li>
        <li>Every change made in the window, from the audit trail</li>
        <li>Printable, and CSV per table</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="plate">
      <div class="plate-in digest">
        <span class="kick">Digest · client.com · 7 days</span>
        <h3>Quiet week, one thing worth knowing.</h3>
        <ul class="dg">
          <li><b>1.92M requests</b>, 97.1% served. Error rate 0.18%, down from 0.31%.</li>
          <li><b>Traffic:</b> US 61%, CA 12%, DE 9%. Top path <code>/</code>, then <code>/blog/spring-launch</code>.</li>
          <li><b>Firewall:</b> 41,200 requests challenged or blocked, 38,900 of them from three sources scanning for <code>/.env</code>.</li>
          <li><b>Alerts:</b> one — origin latency, Tuesday 03:10, resolved in 9 minutes.</li>
          <li><b>Changes:</b> two — a managed-challenge rule (approved by Pierre, Tue), a cache rule for <code>/assets/*</code> (Thu).</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="dg-foot"><span class="chan">Printable page</span><span class="chan">traffic.csv</span><span class="chan">paths.csv</span><span class="chan">firewall.csv</span><span class="chan">changes.csv</span></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption><span><b>Plate VI.</b> Seven days, read back</span><span>Reports</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
